# Example 09: the four nucleic-acid representations, same view each time.
# sgRNA and target DNA from 4OO8 with the protein removed.
#
# Pick by how much base detail the argument needs:
#   ladder     overviews. Backbone plus a thin rung. Cheapest to read.
#   slab       when base stacking or a kink is the point.
#   fill       close contacts where you must see which base edge is used.
#   atoms      the tightest zooms, chemistry-level detail.
open 4oo8
delete /A,D,E,F
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

color /B lab_sgrna
color /C lab_target
view
view pad 0.05

nucleotides nucleic ladder radius 0.35
2dlabels text "ladder" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 24 color lab_black bold true
save na_ladder.png width 1200 supersample 3

2dlabels delete all
nucleotides nucleic slab shape box
2dlabels text "slab" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 24 color lab_black bold true
save na_slab.png width 1200 supersample 3

2dlabels delete all
nucleotides nucleic fill
show nucleic atoms
style nucleic stick
2dlabels text "fill" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 24 color lab_black bold true
save na_fill.png width 1200 supersample 3

2dlabels delete all
nucleotides nucleic atoms
show nucleic atoms
style nucleic stick
2dlabels text "atoms" xpos 0.04 ypos 0.94 size 24 color lab_black bold true
save na_atoms.png width 1200 supersample 3
